1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,080
GOLD measures the upper atmosphere,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:07,030
which is directly affected by the sun
and what we call space weather.

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:10,720
Scientists are working to better
be able to predict space weather

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:14,100
because it directly affects
the safety of our satellites,

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,600
the health of our astronauts,

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,800
and the technologies that we

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,133
use every day in our life
like GPS navigation.

8
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,293
GOLD will be sitting twenty
two thousand miles above Earth,

9
00:00:23,293 --> 00:00:26,073
which means that it can see
a whole half of the Earth,

10
00:00:26,073 --> 00:00:28,223
all of the Western Hemisphere.

11
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:31,373
And it will be hovering over one
particular point on Earth,

12
00:00:31,373 --> 00:00:35,000
watching the dynamics
of the atmosphere play out below.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,050
I am excited about this mission
because GOLD will be getting information

14
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:42,020
about the upper atmosphere
much faster than ever before,

15
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,050
and we'll be able to look

16
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,490
at effects that are more like

17
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:46,967
the weather that we
experience down here on Earth.

18
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:51,182
The GOLD and ICON missions will give
scientists the most comprehensive view

19
00:00:51,182 --> 00:00:53,722
we've ever had of the upper atmosphere.
